# Release and CI/CD pipeline

## Workflows

| Workflow | Trigger | Publishes? |
|----------|---------|------------|
| `ci.yml` | Push/PR to `main` (skips docs/`.cursor`-only via `paths-ignore`) | No — test, lint, GoReleaser snapshot build (`--skip=publish`), Trivy FS vuln scan |
| `docker.yml` | Dockerfile path changes | No — Hadolint + Dockerfile Trivy config scan |
| `release.yml` | CI success on push to `main` (`workflow_call`); tag `vX.Y.Z` push | Yes — GoReleaser binaries, GH release, GHCR via `dockers_v2` |

Do not change CI checks/workflows just to make failures pass. Fix the code or config causing the failure.

## Push to `main` (snapshot)

- **CI** runs on the push (unless only markdown / `.cursor` / `docs` paths changed); **Release** runs after test, lint, GoReleaser snapshot build, and Trivy succeed (not on PR runs).
- Release creates an **immutable** git tag `<latest-vX.Y.Z>-snapshot.<N>` (e.g. `v0.2.0-snapshot.1`, then `.2`, …) via `scripts/next-snapshot-tag.sh` — never force-pushed.
- Runs `goreleaser release --clean` (not `--snapshot`) so `dockers_v2` can push multi-arch manifests.
- `GORELEASER_CURRENT_TAG` set to that numbered snapshot tag; `SKIP_BEFORE_TEST=1` skips GoReleaser `before` `go test` (CI already tested).
- GitHub prerelease + module SBOM via GoReleaser (`release.prerelease: auto`)
- GHCR publish order (scan-before-mutable-tag):
  1. GoReleaser pushes immutable `ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:sha-<commit>`
  2. Trivy scans that digest (`CRITICAL`/`HIGH`, `exit-code: 1`)
  3. Only then promote `v0.2.0-snapshot.N` **and** floating `v0.2.0-snapshot` (snapshot) or semver + `major.minor` + `latest` (full release)
- Cosign + container SBOM after promote; Dockerfile config scan owned by `docker.yml` (Dockerfile path changes)

```bash
docker pull ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:v0.2.0-snapshot      # floating latest on line
docker pull ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:v0.2.0-snapshot.3    # specific build
```

## Tag `vX.Y.Z` push (release)

- GoReleaser: `release --clean` (runs `go test` in `before` hooks — not skipped)
- Docker GHCR: push `sha-<commit>`, Trivy scan, then promote semver (`0.1.2`) + `major.minor` + `latest`
- Full release assets + signed SBOM bundle

```bash
docker pull ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:0.1.2
docker pull ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:latest
```

## When editing `release.yml`

- Keep job-level `permissions` scoped per job (`permissions: {}` at workflow level).
- GoReleaser owns binary build and GHCR push in one job (QEMU + Buildx + GHCR login before `release --clean`).
- Snapshot vs release tagging is driven by `is_snapshot` / `release_tag` / `image_tag` job outputs — do not hardcode version strings in the workflow.
- Tag trigger must be `v[0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+` so `v*-snapshot.N` tags do not re-enter Release as a full release.
- Mutable image tags must never be updated before a successful Trivy image scan of the digest.
- Trivy steps that run in the same job as GoReleaser must set `cache-dir` outside the workspace (e.g. `${{ runner.temp }}/trivy-cache`); the action default is `${{ github.workspace }}/.cache/trivy` and will dirty the git tree.

## Tests in release path

GoReleaser `before` hooks run `go test -buildvcs=false ./...` unless `SKIP_BEFORE_TEST=1` (set on CI `workflow_call` only). Tag pushes and local runs always test. Add unit tests for release-related logic (path resolution, tagging helpers) rather than relying on manual Omni credentials in CI.

## SBOM sources of truth

| Artifact | Owner |
|----------|--------|
| Module `sbom.cyclonedx.json` | GoReleaser (`sboms`); local `make sbom` |
| Image `sbom-image.cyclonedx.json` | `release.yml` Trivy after publish |
| CI | Trivy FS **vuln** scan only — no overlapping SBOM artifact uploads |
